<%- include('partials/head') %>
<body class="hub">
  <main class="hub-main">
    <p class="eyebrow">The Royal Knot · UI module</p>
    <h1 class="display"><%= typeof notFound !== 'undefined' ? 'That page isn’t here' : 'Developer preview' %></h1>
    <p class="lede">Two separate interfaces, rendered from mock data in the browser. Nothing here signs in, saves, sends, or charges anything.</p>
    <div class="hub-grid">
      <a class="hub-card" href="/couple">
        <span class="hub-tag">Client-facing</span>
        <h2>Couple portal</h2>
        <p>Share planning details, book a consultation, follow the journey, and preview later modules: requirements, vendor shortlist, agreement, payments, and events.</p>
        <span class="hub-go">Open couple portal →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="hub-card hub-card-dark" href="/agent/weddings">
        <span class="hub-tag">Internal</span>
        <h2>Agent workspace</h2>
        <p>Wedding cases, workspace dashboard, meeting and notes, documents, agreement, vendor proposals, tasks, schedule, finance, and season overview.</p>
        <span class="hub-go">Open agent workspace →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="hub-foot">Presenting? Add <code>?stage=0</code> … <code>?stage=9</code> to the couple portal or a wedding workspace to show a planning stage. Developer controls stay hidden unless you add <code>?dev=1</code> (turn off with <code>?dev=0</code>).</p>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
